@startuml data-model
title Class diagram — Express Voitures (data model)

hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #34495E
  ArrowColor #34495E
}

class Brand {
  -id : Integer
  -name : String
}

class CarModel {
  -id : Integer
  -name : String
}

class Trim {
  -id : Integer
  -name : String
}

class VehicleSpecification {
  -id : Integer
}

class Vehicle {
  -id : Integer
  -vin : String [0..1]
  -year : Integer
  -purchaseDate : Date
  -purchasePrice : Decimal
  -availabilityDate : Date [0..1]
  -saleDate : Date [0..1]
  -description : String [0..1]
  -photoUrl : String [0..1]
  --
  +/margin : Decimal
  +/repairsCost : Decimal
  +/salePrice : Decimal
  +/isAvailable : Boolean
  +/designation : String
}

class Repair {
  -id : Integer
  -description : String
  -cost : Decimal
}

class IdentityUser <<ASP.NET Identity>> #EEEEEE {
  -id : String
  -email : String
}

note right of Vehicle
  {A Vehicle is one **physical unit** in stock,
  not a catalogue category.}

  {salePrice = purchasePrice + repairsCost + margin}
  {margin is not persisted: supplied from
  configuration when the vehicle is read,
  500 EUR by default}
  {repairsCost, salePrice, isAvailable and
  designation are derived: computed on read,
  never stored as columns}

  {saleDate empty = still for sale}
end note

note bottom of Repair
  {A Repair is a first-class entity: the client's
  spreadsheet packed several repairs into one cell,
  which is not atomic.}
end note

note right of IdentityUser
  {Single manager account. No association with the
  inventory: one user administers everything.}
end note

note left of Trim
  {(carModel, name) is unique}

  {Brand, CarModel and Trim are the three levels of
  one catalogue hierarchy. Extracting the first two
  and keeping the third as free text would be
  inconsistent. A trim belongs to a model: "LE" at
  Mazda is unrelated to "LE" at another make,
  hence uniqueness per model, not globally.}
end note

note left of Brand
  {name is unique}
end note

note right of CarModel
  {(brand, name) is unique}
end note

note right of VehicleSpecification
  {Carries the (brand, model, trim) triple as one key.
  A Vehicle holds only this key, so each characteristic
  is one join away instead of traversing
  Vehicle -> Trim -> CarModel -> Brand.}

  {(brand, carModel, trim) is unique}

  {Composite foreign keys make an inconsistent triple
  impossible: (carModel, brand) must exist in CarModel,
  and (trim, carModel) must exist in Trim. The database
  refuses "Ford + Civic", not the application.}
end note

' ---- Layout: Brand > CarModel > Trim stacked on the left, facing
' ---- VehicleSpecification on the right so the three associations to it
' ---- run horizontally without crossing. Vehicle below, Repair further down.
Brand -[hidden]down- CarModel
CarModel -[hidden]down- Trim
CarModel -[hidden]right- VehicleSpecification
VehicleSpecification -[hidden]down- Vehicle
Vehicle -[hidden]down- Repair
Repair -[hidden]right- IdentityUser

Brand "1" -- "0..*" CarModel : offers >
CarModel "1" -- "0..*" Trim : comes as >
Brand "1" -- "0..*" VehicleSpecification
CarModel "1" -- "0..*" VehicleSpecification
Trim "1" -- "0..*" VehicleSpecification
VehicleSpecification "1" -- "0..*" Vehicle : stocked as >
Vehicle "1" *-- "0..*" Repair : undergoes >

legend bottom right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | 1 | exactly one |
  | 0..1 | zero or one (optional) |
  | 0..* | zero to many |
  | / | derived attribute, not persisted |
  | filled diamond | composition: the part cannot exist without the whole |
  Read a multiplicity at the end //opposite// the class you start from.
  Foreign keys are not shown as attributes: the associations carry them.
  A Vehicle reaches its Brand, CarModel and Trim through its
  Specification: one join away, instead of the former chain
  Vehicle -> Trim -> CarModel -> Brand.

  |= English |= Français |
  | Brand | marque |
  | CarModel | modèle |
  | Trim | finition |
  | VehicleSpecification | spécification (marque + modèle + finition) |
  | Vehicle | véhicule (exemplaire en stock) |
  | Repair | réparation |
  | purchasePrice / salePrice | prix d'achat / prix de vente |
  | repairsCost | coût des réparations |
  | margin | marge |
  | designation | désignation |
  | availabilityDate / saleDate | date de disponibilité / date de vente |
endlegend

@enduml
